1. User management

IAM -> identity access management

User, Group, Role, Permissions
A group has multiple users
A user have specific role
A role will have permissions

ramesh, he joined devops team, he has trainee role, trainee role has particular permissions

roles/sub-groups
===========
devops-trainee -> only read access -> ramesh will be added to this group
devops-juniors -> he can do specific writes -> ramesh will be moved to this group
devops-seniors -> he can write and update
devops-leads   -> he can write, update and delete

create user -> linux user must have 1 primiary group, and 0-many secondary groups
useradd <user-name> -> creates user and group with same name
id <user-name>
/etc/passwd -> user information
/etc/group -> group information

groupadd <group-name>

usermod -g <group-name> <user-name> -> -g means primary group
usermod -G <group-name> <user-name> -> adding secondary group
usermod -aG <group-name> <user-name> -> appending secondary group to user

passwd <user-name>

